<title>INDIA: India's Voltas records 1996/97 loss.</title>
<headline>India's Voltas records 1996/97 loss.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit/loss	 (168.2)   vs    157.0</p>
<p>    Sales		   14,694.0    vs 14,594.6</p>
<p>    Gross profit	     557.9    vs    690.1</p>
<p>    Financial items	  453.3    vs    312.6</p>
<p>    Cash profit		104.6    vs    377.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     227.5    vs    189.6</p>
<p>Write-off of deferred</p>
<p>    revenue expenditure     45.0    vs     30.3</p>
<p>    Taxation		     0.3    vs	0.6</p>
<p>    Dividend (in percent)  nil	vs     25.0</p>
<p>Note: Voltas Limited said it incurred losses due to a significant slowdown in the demand for white goods coupled with increases in installed capacities. The company said sales and other income include profit on property sales amounting to 130 million rupees.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22 265 9000</p>
</text>
